scenario_text:
Context from Monday.com — Upfront Tracker 2026-2027:
Client: 'Meridian Financial Group' (via Publicis) | Total commitment: $4.2M | Package: 'Total Audience' bundle | Breakdown: Linear (Prism Cable Network) 55% / Streaming (PrismStream+) 45% | Pricing model: Blended CPM across platforms at $26 | Guarantee: A25-54, combined 2.1 GRP equivalent | Status: 'Signed May 2026'

Context from NetSuite — Internal P&L View:
Prism Cable Network (Linear): Margin floor = 62% | Cost basis per unit = $9.50 CPM equivalent
PrismStream+ (Streaming): Margin floor = 45% | Cost basis per unit = $14.80 CPM equivalent
[Controller note, Q1 2026]: 'Streaming and Linear are separate cost centers per board directive effective Jan 2026. Cross-subsidization no longer permitted for margin reporting.'

Context from Google Doc — 'Upfront Deal Approval Matrix v2.1' (updated May 2026):
Section 6: 'Blended cross-platform deals must meet minimum margin at the TOTAL DEAL level (55%).'
[VERSION HISTORY: v2.0 (Jan 2026) read: 'must meet minimum margin at each platform level independently.' Changed to 'total deal level' in v2.1 per Sales leadership request, May 15 2026.]

Context from Slack — #sales-planning (Jun 4, 2026, 11:22 AM):
@rachel.nakamura: Finance flagged the Meridian deal. At $26 blended CPM with 45% streaming mix, the streaming portion alone runs at 43% margin — below the 45% floor.
@alex.petrov: But v2.1 of the approval matrix says total deal level, not per-platform.
@rachel.nakamura: Right, and at total deal level it's ~54.8%. Still below the 55% total floor by a hair.
@alex.petrov: When was the deal signed?
@rachel.nakamura: May 22.
@alex.petrov: And v2.1 was published May 15. So it was under v2.1 rules.
@rachel.nakamura: But the board directive on cross-subsidization is separate from the approval matrix. That's a finance policy, not a sales policy.

Context from Slack — #finance-ops (Jun 5, 2026, 3:18 PM):
@cfo_office: For the avoidance of doubt — the Jan 2026 board directive on P&L separation supersedes any sales policy that permits blended margin calculation across cost centers. Deals must be profitable at each cost center independently.
@rachel.nakamura: :white_check_mark:
@tomas.reyes: Does this apply retroactively to signed upfronts?
[No reply in thread]

Context from HubSpot CRM:
Deal: 'Meridian Financial — 26-27 Upfront' | Value: $4.2M | Signed: May 22, 2026 | IO Reference: IO-2026-0447 | Special terms: 'Platform allocation may shift +/-10% at Prism's discretion for delivery optimization.'

Context from Google Sheets — 'Streaming Inventory Forecast Q3 2026':
PrismStream+ available premium impressions: 82% sold | Standard: 71% sold | Note: 'Tight Q3. Make-goods from Q2 under-deliveries consuming 8% of premium pool.'
